To do, in order

[ ] 1. Generic block + model forward
      What: the block and the model now carry the residual *state* (today just the [T, D]
        tensor h, i.e. the old x) and go through residual.read / residual.write instead of
        `x = x + ...`. Same math as before; the golden test later proves it.
      Contract:
        DecoderBlock.forward(state, residual, meta, layer_cache) -> (state, aux)
          mixer is sublayer i = first, ffn is i = first + 1. For each:
            input = its norm(residual.read(state, i))
            update, sub_aux = mixer(input, meta, layer_cache)   /   ffn(input, meta)   (positional)
            state = residual.write(state, i, update)
          aux = empty AuxOutputs + mixer aux under "mixer" + ffn aux under "ffn"
        TransformerLM.forward(meta, paged_kv_caches=None) -> ModelOutputs
          state = self.residual.init(embedding(meta.token_ids))
          each block: state, block_aux = block(state, self.residual, meta, that layer's cache);
                      merge block_aux under "layers.{idx}"
          logits, head_aux = self.head(self.residual.final(state), meta); merge under "head"
      Files: model/decoder_block.py, model/model.py
      Done: pytest tests/test_model_contracts.py passes, except the post_step test (item 4).
      Status (desktop copy, 2026-10-07 07:20): __init__ done. Left:
        decoder_block.py:51,62  pass sublayer inputs positionally (MoE has no `state`/`batch_meta` params)
        decoder_block.py:58     write(state, ...), not write(residual, ...)
        model.py:55             state = self.residual.init(<embedding output>); `x` no longer exists
        model.py:62             pass the object: residual=self.residual
        model.py:69             head input is self.residual.final(state)

[ ] 2. Convert the golden checkpoint (D17). Nothing to write, just run:
